# checks that domains are case-insensitive in the database
depends append
# appends a message exactly like uid 1 to the mailbox, except with
# different case on the addresses.
send 6
a append INBOX () {123+}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@ORYX.COM>
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@Oryx.Com>
Date: Thu, 13 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

asdf
receive 4
* 5 EXISTS
* 5 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 6] next uid
a OK [APPENDUID 1 5] done
# check that we can search properly on all
send 1
b1 search from @oryx.com
receive 2
* SEARCH 1 2 3 4 5
b1 OK done
send 1
b2 search from @ORYX.COM
receive 2
* SEARCH 1 2 3 4 5
b2 OK done
send 1
c fetch 1,5 rfc822
# ... and expect the two to be identical when they come back.
# (we actually expect the first casing seen to be used for both messages.)
receive 17
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS (\Recent \Seen))
* 5 FETCH (UID 5 FLAGS (\Recent \Seen))
* 1 FETCH (RFC822 {125}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@oryx.com>
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@oryx.com>
Date: Thu, 13 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

asdf
)
* 5 FETCH (RFC822 {125}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@oryx.com>
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@oryx.com>
Date: Thu, 13 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

asdf
)
c OK done
end
